  ============================================================================
  Dark Roast: House Blend — iTerm2 Color Scheme
  Version: 5.1.0 Companion

  WHAT IS THIS
  ——————
  A complete iTerm2 color scheme (.itermcolors) implementing the Dark Roast
  design system's ANSI-16 palette. Covers all 16 ANSI colors plus every iTerm2
  chrome key (background, foreground, cursor, selection, bold, badge, tab, link).

  INSTALL
  ———-
  Option A (easiest — double-click):
    1. Double-click "Dark Roast House Blend.itermcolors" in Finder
       (or: open "Dark Roast House Blend.itermcolors" from Terminal)
    2. iTerm2 will import it automatically under Preferences →
       Profiles → Colors → Color Presets → "Dark Roast House Blend"
    3. Select it from the Color Presets dropdown in your profile

  Option B (manual import):
    1. iTerm2 → Settings (⌘,) → Profiles → Colors
    2. Click "Color Presets..." dropdown → "Import..."
    3. Select this file
    4. Select "Dark Roast House Blend" from the Color Presets dropdown

  Option C (apply to all profiles):
    Import as above, then go to each profile and select the preset.
    To set as default for new sessions, update the "Default" profile.

  ABOUT THE FORMAT
  ————————
  iTerm2 stores colors as XML plists where each color is a dict with five keys:
    Alpha Component  — float 0.0–1.0  (1.0 = fully opaque)
    Blue Component   — float 0.0–1.0
    Color Space      — string ("sRGB" for standard, "P3" for wide-gamut)
    Green Component  — float 0.0–1.0
    Red Component    — float 0.0–1.0

  All Dark Roast colors are specified in sRGB. No P3 wide-gamut is used; the
  palette is designed for warm espresso tones, not high-saturation display-P3.

  PALETTE PHILOSOPHY
  —————————
  All four Dark Roast terminal themes (Warp, Tabby, Terminal.app, iTerm2)
  share an identical ANSI-16 palette so that ls, git diff, vim syntax,
  tmux, and every other CLI tool produce exactly the same output regardless
  of which emulator you're running in.

  FULL COLOR REFERENCE
  ——————————
  Chrome:
    background    #241810   void      — warm-dark deepest layer
    foreground    #FFF8F0   crema     — primary text (16.43:1 contrast vs void)
    cursor        #2CB9AA   teal      — kinetic cursor, matches editor caret
    cursor text   #241810   void      — text inside cursor block (inverted)
    selection bg  #3B2A20   espresso  — warm polished surface (v4: was `grain`)
    selection fg  #FFF8F0   crema     — text color on selection
    bold          #FFF8F0   crema     — bold text color (same hue, higher weight)
    badge         #FE8175   scarlet   — iTerm2 badge/notification
    tab           #2B1D14   obsidian  — tab bar background color
    link          #2CB9AA   teal      — hyperlink color in terminal output

  ANSI Normal (indices 0–7):
    0  black       #2B1D14   obsidian  — dark floor (not as deep as void)
    1  red         #FE8175   scarlet   — error / critical
    2  green       #79B56C   sage      — warm fern (terminal extension)
    3  yellow      #E9922E   amber     — warning / accent
    4  blue        #6AACE2   slate     — dusty steel blue (terminal extension)
    5  magenta     #D28DE2   mauve     — dried lavender (terminal extension)
    6  cyan        #2CB9AA   teal      — live data flow / resolved
    7  white       #E9DCCF   bone      — reduced-contrast light text

  ANSI Bright (indices 8–15):
    8  bright black    #BCA18A   crater-deep — comment gray, tmux inactive (v4: was `crater`)
    9  bright red      #FF9286   scarlet+  — scarlet companion-bright
    10 bright green    #98D083   sage+     — sage companion-bright
    11 bright yellow   #D0A200   gold      — success / stable severity
    12 bright blue     #68C7F4   slate+    — slate companion-bright
    13 bright magenta  #E792DF   mauve+    — mauve companion-bright
    14 bright cyan     #72D8CA   teal+     — teal brightened (lighter than #2CB9AA;
                                             bright should be visibly brighter)
    15 bright white    #FFF8F0   crema     — full brightness
  ============================================================================
-->
